Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/AudioRecordingConfiguration.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), the F4g slice of ADR-0064: the effects of a recording are Objects, none ever.

Why: the effects are AudioEffect.Descriptors, and AudioEffect is a compile-only stub here (its natives and the audio
effect framework are not Minato's), so any array of them (`new AudioEffect.Descriptor[n]`, even of length 0) throws
NoClassDefFoundError when it runs, and no configuration could be made, read from a parcel or listed. Minato has no audio
effects, so the arrays are always empty: they are Object arrays, the getters answer empty lists, and a Descriptor is only
named where an effect would be (the casts in the loops, which do not run for an empty array). A parcel that carries an
effect fails as before with NoClassDefFoundError.

